tara:TARA_0427594 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GB 29" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 186. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "居髎(髎)" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Pain and numbness in the thigh and lumbar region, paralysis, muscular atrophy of the lower limbs." ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "The lateral femoral cutaneous nerve." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "In the buttock region, midpoint of the line connecting the anterior superior iliac spine and the prominence of the greater trochanter." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_5283975 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Juliao" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0002503,
        UBERON:0013708 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0013691 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "G 29",
        "Gallbladder 29" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "The branches of the superficial circumflex iliac artery and vein, the ascending branches of the lateral circumflex femoral artery and vein." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
