tara:TARA_2187225 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "SI 9" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 92. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "肩貞(贞)" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Pain in the scapular region, motor impairment of the hand and arm." ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "The branch of the axillary nerve; deeper in the superior aspect, the radial nerve." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "On the shoulder girdle, posteroinferior to the shoulder joint, 1 B-cun superior to the posterior axillary fold. Note: When the arm is adducted, SI 9 is located 1 B-cun superior to the posterior axillary fold, posterior to the deltoid muscle." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_9093316 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Jianzhen" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0001470,
        UBERON:0001476,
        ILX:0795311 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001421 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "Small Intestine 9" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "The circumflex scapular artery and vein." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty tara:locatedInRelationTo ;
            owl:someValuesFrom [ a owl:Restriction ;
