tara:TARA_3339722 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BL 38" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 118. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "(浮)郄" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Numbness of the gluteal and femoral regions, contracture of the tendons in the popliteal fossa." ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "The posterior femoral cutaneous nerve and the common peroneal nerve." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "On the posterior aspect of the knee, just medial to the biceps femoris tendon, 1 B-cun proximal to the popliteal crease. Note: With the knee in slight flexion, BL38 is located medial to the biceps femoris ten- don, 1 B-cun proximal to BL39." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_7525476 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Fuxi" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0001374,
        ILX:0795317,
        ILX:0795330 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0001465 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "B 38",
        "Bladder 38",
        "UB 38",
        "Urinary Bladder 38" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "The superolateral genicular artery and vein." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
