    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 128. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "承山" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Low back pain, spasm of the gastrocnemius, hemorrhoids, constipation, beriberi." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "On the posterior aspect of the leg, at the connecting point of the calcaneal tendon with the two muscle bellies of the gastrocnemius muscle. Note: With the leg stretched (plantar flexion) or the heel up, BL57 is located at the sharp angled depression inferior to the muscle belly of the gastrocnemius muscle. the two heads of the gastrocnemius muscle are separated to make a lambda shape (Λ)." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_7525476 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Chengshan" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0001388,
        UBERON:0003701 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0003823 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "B 57",
        "Bladder 57",
        "UB 57",
        "Urinary Bladder 57" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "See Chengjin (BL 56)." ;
