tara:TARA_5102514 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GB 11" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 177. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "頭(头)竅(窍)陰(阴)" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Pain of the head and neck, tinnitus, deafness, pain in the ears." ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "The anastomotic branch of the great and lesser occipital nerves." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "On the head, posterior and superior to the mastoid process, at the junction of the up- per two thirds and lower one third of the curved line from gB 9 to gB12." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_5283975 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Touqiaoyin" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0011220 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0000033 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "G 11",
        "Gallbladder 11" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "The branches of the posterior auricular artery and vein." ;
