    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 67. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "衝(冲)陽(阳)" ;
    tara:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole tara:TARA_1840369 ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Pain of the upper teeth, redness and swelling of the dorsum of the foot, facial paralysis, muscular atrophy and motor impairment of the foot." ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "Superficially, the medial dorsal cutaneous nerve of foot derived from the superficial peroneal nerve; deeper, the deep peroneal nerve." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "On the dorsum of the foot, at the joint of the base of the second metatarsal bone and the intermediate cuneiform bone, over the dorsalis pedis artery." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_6221269 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Avoid puncturing the artery." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Chongyang" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0001453,
