tara:TARA_8557069 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "GV 4" ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 205. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "命門(门)" ;
    tara:hasIndicationsDescription "Stiffness of the back, lumbago, impotence, nocturnal emission, irregular menstruation, diarrhea, indigestion, leukorrhea." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "In the lumbar region, in the depression inferior to the spinous process of the second lumbar vertebra (L2), on the posterior median line." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_0386099 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Mingmen" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0004618,
        ILX:0795312 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0005462 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "Du 4",
