    dcterms:bibliographicCitation """Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 205. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.""" ;
    tara:hasChineseLabel "腰陽(阳)關(关,関)" ;
    tara:hasInnervationDescription "The medial branch of the posterior ramus of the lumbar nerve." ;
    tara:hasLocationalDescription "In the lumbar region, in the depression inferior to the spinous process of the fourth lumbar vertebra (L4), on the posterior median line. Note: GV 3 can be located by first palpating the highest points of the iliac crests and the spinous process of the fourth lumbar vertebra (L4) can then be found at the midpoint of the highest points of both iliac crests." ;
    tara:hasMeridian tara:TARA_0386099 ;
    tara:hasMethodDescription "Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable." ;
    tara:hasPinyinLabel "Yaoyangguan" ;
    tara:hasRelatedLocation UBERON:0004620,
        UBERON:0014437,
        ILX:0795312 ;
    tara:hasSurfaceLocation UBERON:0005462 ;
    tara:hasSynonym "Du 3",
        "Governor Vessel 3" ;
    tara:hasVasculatureDescription "The posterior branch of the lumbar artery." ;
